  m_text: "The\_Panzerkampfwagen VI Ausf\xFChrung H1 (Tiger H1)\_is the first (early-production)
    variant of the Tiger I heavy tank family, designed and built by Henschel and
    used by the German Army during World War II. It offered the German Army its first
    armoured fighting vehicle equipped with the 88 mm Kampfwagenkanone (KwK) 36 tank
    gun, developed from the 88 mm Flugabwehrkanone (FlaK) 36 anti-aircraft gun.\r\nWeight:\r\n54
    Tonnes\r\n57 Tonnes(Combat weight)\r\nLength\r\n6.30m\r\nHight\r\n3.00m"
